  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investing for Impact Against Tuberculosis - Nigeria (01-Jan-2024-31-Dec-2026)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigeria, Tuberculosis, National Tuberculosis &amp; Leprosy Control Programme (NTBLCP)This program has the following goals: To accelerate efforts at ending TB epidemic in Nigeria by ensuring access to comprehensive and high quality patients&apos; centered and community owned TB (TB. TB/HIV and DR-TB) services for all Nigerians by 2026. The objectives of this program are: To increase case notification rate of all forms of TB from 131/100,000 population in 2022 to 142/100,000 population in 2026.  To sustain TB treatment success rate beyond the NSP 2021-2026 target of 90% during the grant period.  To enrol 100% of diagnosed DR-TB patients on appropriate treatment by 2026</narrative>
  </description>
